+        # Before the request has more blocks than a complete lookup window,
+        # _sliding_window_lookup falls back to the contiguous prefix. Every
+        # leading block is therefore reachable. This is especially important
+        # for EAGLE prompts with a partial trailing block: the EAGLE peek moves
+        # the replay-boundary tail one block to the right, but the unavailable
+        # peek is capped by the key list on lookup, which then needs the whole
+        # prefix instead.
+        if end_block <= need:
+            return None
         # The matched run's right edge sits on the aligned boundary block when
         # EAGLE peeks one block past it (shift=1), otherwise on the last block
         # before the boundary (shift=0).
